        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: கடப்பாடு",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "கடப்பாடு — kaṭappāṭu — \"an obligation; a commitment\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "கொடுத்த வாக்கைக் காப்பாற்றுவது நம் கடப்பாடு. koṭutta vākkaik kāppāṟṟuvatu nam kaṭappāṭu. Keeping our word is our obligation."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A formal word close to கடமை, duty; கடமை and கடன், a debt, share one root."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "கடப்பாடு (kaṭappāṭu) is native: DEDR 1113 lists Tamil kaṭaṉ, \"obligation, debt\", and kaṭamai, \"duty\"; the word is usually read as that root joined to pāṭu, the noun of paṭu: the state of being bound. DEDR does not list kaṭappāṭu itself."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
